      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are right to be concerned about what you are teaching your child, and the focus should be on fundamental values like respect and kindness. You can explain that people are diverse, just like in any community, and that everyone deserves to be treated with dignity. When it comes to pronouns, you can teach your child to be polite and use the pronouns someone asks you to use, framing it as a simple act of courtesy. This approach teaches respect without requiring you to adopt complex ideological stances.",
